{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVbisG1FAWGEY2W4bJrC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GptDUek1he8gb14yy3N8Hq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='paper.tex'; s=open(p).read()\nreps=[\n(\"(i) A refit-verified, influence-ordered protocol for leaderboard fragility. It covers\",\n \"(i) A measurement protocol for leaderboard fragility built on a refit-verified, influence-ordered perturbation finder; the finder is the provided baseline (starter) configuration, not a new algorithm of ours. The protocol covers\"),\n(\"The protocol is cheap. All 17 cases, including the 135,622-row Arena case, completed in about 16\\\\,s of recorded episode time per seed (15.5--16.3\\\\,s). This covers data transfer, the search, and the evaluator's verification refit, and it is possible because each refit acts on $p\\\\times p$ sufficient statistics.\",\n \"The protocol appears cheap. The recorded episode time per seed, over all 17 cases including the 135,622-row Arena case, was about 16\\\\,s (15.5--16.3\\\\,s). The record does not state what this time includes, and we did not profile it; a plausible but unmeasured reason for the low cost is that each refit acts on $p\\\\times p$ sufficient statistics.\"),\n(\"was 15.99\\\\,s, 15.55\\\\,s, and 16.33\\\\,s. This includes data transfer, the search, and the evaluator's verification refit.\",\n \"was 15.99\\\\,s, 15.55\\\\,s, and 16.33\\\\,s. The evaluation record gives one duration per seed and does not specify which steps it covers.\"),\n(\"Recorded episode time was about 16\\\\,s per seed; the evaluator's comparator runs add to this.\",\n \"Recorded episode time was about 16\\\\,s per seed; the record does not specify which harness steps (e.g., comparator runs or verification refits) this duration includes.\"),\n(\"(identical to the baseline tree);\",\n \"(the provided baseline starter configuration, byte-identical to the baseline tree);\"),\n(\"An autonomous LLM-based research agent proposed the study design within the task's constraints. It implemented the perturbation finder and the refined configurations, wrote the analysis and plotting scripts, and drafted this manuscript, including its framing and text.\",\n \"An autonomous LLM-based research agent proposed the study design within the task's constraints. The evaluated perturbation finder was not written by the agent: it is the provided starter (baseline) configuration, seeded before the search. The agent designed three refined search configurations, but their source is not among our artifacts and none was scored. The agent wrote the analysis and plotting scripts and drafted this manuscript, including its framing and text.\"),\n]\nfor a,b in reps:\n    assert s.count(a)==1, a[:60]\n    s=s.replace(a,b)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n -i \"implement\" paper.tex | head; grep -n -i \"transfer\\|our finder\\|we implement\\|our instrument\" paper.tex | head","description":"Apply targeted repairs for both audit findings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1117,"cache_read_input_tokens":52797,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1117},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6af20b8-3edd-4696-ac58-f407db387098","uuid":"3164da9a-31e4-4abb-9003-79958cd67a8a","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:42:00.786Z","request_id":"req_011CgVbirfXmZSA2ivDBE3ye"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GptDUek1he8gb14yy3N8Hq","type":"tool_result","content":"90:where $\\sigma$ is the logistic function and ties count as half a win for each side. The ridge weight $\\lambda$ and the tolerance $\\tau$ below are passed to the finder by the evaluation harness with each request; the harness specifies $\\lambda=0.1$ and $\\tau=10^{-6}$. The ridge term fixes the location of $\\theta$ and keeps the fit finite even when the perturbation removes all of a player's losses. According to the harness's stated protocol, players with fewer than 50 comparisons are removed iteratively before fitting. The player set is then fixed: a player keeps its index even if every one of its rows is dropped. Equation~\\eqref{eq:bt} depends on the data only through the $p\\times p$ matrices of (half-)wins $W_{ij}$ and counts $N_{ij}$. A refit after any perturbation therefore costs $O(p^3)$ per Newton step, independent of $n$. The finder's refit implements exactly this objective (source locations in Appendix~\\ref{app:repro}).\n360:Three refined search configurations were designed to target that improvement. As recorded, they are relinearized category-knapsack variants: one with multi-pair targeting and pruning, one with swap refinement, and one with pruning seeded from the baseline influence set. No source for these configurations is among our artifacts, so we give no further implementation detail. All three were unscored (0 of 3 scored), and the evaluation evidence does not record why. Their effect on $\\kver$ is unknown and should not be read as a loss. No result in the main text depends on them.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6af20b8-3edd-4696-ac58-f407db387098","uuid":"1c211c7f-a6c5-4b8d-891c-32c155390399","timestamp":"2026-10-29T00:42:00.907Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"90:where $\\sigma$ is the logistic function and ties count as half a win for each side. The ridge weight $\\lambda$ and 